<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raman Skirmunt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1868">1868</a>–<a href="/years/1939">1939</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Roman Skirmunt</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Raman Skirmunt was a Belarusian landowner and politician, a member of the first Russian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-duma">State Duma</a>. In 1918 he briefly headed the government of the Belarusian Democratic Republic. He was killed in September 1939, after the Soviet invasion of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/raman-skirmunt.jpg" alt="Raman Skirmunt" width="320" height="421" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roman_Skirmunt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
